From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 20:36:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: ipad5: Arm cover line 10 only; name the
 backlight LED driver

Only event 0x30 (PMIC GPIO line 0) was listed as a wake event, but that
is not the line iOS wakes on, and it latches at every sleep whether a
cover moves or not, also in pm_test runs that never leave the device
phase. At sleep entry AppleD2365PMU unmasks the GPIO events of the lines
whose configuration byte passes cfg & 0xc1 == 1 (sleep entry at
0xfffffff006bbb380). On a cold-booted J71t the boot firmware leaves line
0 at 0x24 and line 10 at 0x25 (logged by the PMIC GPIO driver,
2026-11-11), so iOS arms line 10 (event 0x3a) and not line 0; a cover
move latches both lines. Arm 0x3a alone. The polled cover switches read
both lines as before.

The backlight's enable is the LP8559 at I2C0 0x26 (ADT i2c0/lp8559, the
target of /backlight function-backlight_enable). Describe it and point the
DWI backlight at it, so that a dark panel is off.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Berkay Kösebay <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Link: https://github.com/OrchardLinux/orchard/pull/231#issuecomment-7138590680
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s800x-ipad5.dtsi | 21 +++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s800x-ipad5.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s800x-ipad5.dtsi
index 6c252bb..de0a7b5 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s800x-ipad5.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s800x-ipad5.dtsi
@@ -147,6 +147,11 @@
 		       "0", "0", "-1";
 };
 
+/* ADT /backlight function-backlight_enable is the LP8559's ("bklE"). */
+&dwi_bl {
+	apple,led-driver = <&backlight_led>;
+};
+
 &framebuffer0 {
 	power-domains = <&ps_disp0 &ps_dp>;
 };
@@ -167,6 +172,12 @@
 &i2c0 {
 	status = "okay";
 
+	/* ADT i2c0/lp8559: the backlight LED driver; DWI sends its levels. */
+	backlight_led: backlight@26 {
+		compatible = "ti,lp8559";
+		reg = <0x26>;
+	};
+
 	tristar: port-controller@1a {
 		compatible = "nxp,cbtl1610";
 		reg = <0x1a>;
@@ -190,8 +201,14 @@
 			interrupt-controller;
 			#interrupt-cells = <2>;
 			interrupts-extended = <&pinctrl_ap 76 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW>;
-			/* Smart Cover front hall sensor (line 0): wake only. */
-			apple,wake-events = <0x30>;
+			/*
+			 * Smart Cover hall sensors (lines 0 and 10): wake only,
+			 * as iOS arms them: line 10 alone (its boot
+			 * configuration 0x25 passes the sleep rule
+			 * cfg & 0xc1 == 1; line 0's 0x24 does not). Line 0
+			 * latches at every sleep, with or without a cover.
+			 */
+			apple,wake-events = <0x3a>;
 		};
 
 		tristar_charger: charger@180 {
